  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "Setpoint exceedance for two of the SRV pilot stage assemblies (A and J) is attributed to corrosion bonding between the pilot discs and seating surfaces, which is consistent with industry experience. The cause of the R SRV Main failing to actuate is attributed to the main disc and piston thread wear, resulting in side-loading of the main piston within the guide, allowing slight grooves to form in the guide in which the piston and rings could bind.",
    "cause_code": "B",
    "category": "Design/Manufacturing/Installation",
    "theme": "SRV pilot corrosion bonding and main-stage piston/thread wear causing setpoint drift and failure to lift",
    "provisional": false
  },
