  "chain": "corrosion bonding at pilot disc/seat [cause B] -> SRV pilot setpoint drift (F013A, F013J) -> TS 3.4.2.1 inoperability; separately: main disc/piston thread wear -> piston side-loading -> guide grooving/ring binding -> R SRV main valve fails to lift -> two-or-more SRVs inoperable, TS 3.4.2.1 Action (a) reportable condition",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two independent, parallel failure mechanisms converge on the same TS 3.4.2.1 reportability consequence: (1) corrosion-bonding-driven pilot setpoint drift on 2-stage SRVs F013A/F013J, and (2) thread wear/side-loading/grooving causing the R (3-stage) SRV main valve to fail to lift. Both are modeled as separate chains CAUSED_BY the same official cause code B (Design/Manufacturing/Installation), per the narrative's cause statement covering both mechanisms. No operable backup system is named for SRV function in this narrative (safety significance argued via design margins, not a backup system), so no BACKED_UP_BY edge is asserted. Previous-occurrence LERs are modeled as stubs per instructions, using LER numbers exactly as stated in text (including revision suffixes where given)."
